1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Software" or "Work" means the source code, object code,
documentation, configuration, scripts, examples, and other
copyrightable material released by [COPYRIGHT HOLDER] under this
License, together with any portion of that material.

1.2 "Original Work" means the Work as originally released by
Alexander License under this License, including subsequent official
versions, but excluding material identified as subject to a separate
third-party license.

1.3 "Derivative Work" means a work based upon, incorporating,
adapting, translating, or otherwise transforming the Original Work or
a substantial portion of it, to the extent it qualifies as a
derivative work under applicable copyright law.

A work that merely interoperates with the Work, implements an
interface, calls a public API, or independently reimplements
functionality WITHOUT copying or adapting protectable expression is
NOT, solely for those reasons, a Derivative Work. Copyright protects
expression, not ideas, functions, or interfaces — an independently
written implementation of the same function, algorithm, or interface
is not a Derivative Work merely because it serves the same purpose.

1.4 "Modification" means an alteration, adaptation, translation,
rewrite, refactoring, or other change to PRE-EXISTING material from
the Work — whether made by editing that material in place or by
copying, relocating, or adapting it into another file, module, or
section. Renaming a file or relocating copied code does not, by
itself, convert a Modification into a New Original Contribution.

A Modification does NOT include material genuinely authored from
scratch that does not copy, adapt, translate, or incorporate
pre-existing expressive material from the Work.

1.5 "New Original Contribution" means a file, module, function,
class, or other material authored entirely from scratch by a
Contributor, containing no copied, adapted, translated, or otherwise
incorporated pre-existing expressive material from the Work. Merely
using documented APIs, interfaces, protocols, ideas, or algorithms
considered at an abstract level does not, by itself, make
independently authored material a Modification.

1.6 "Contributor" means any person or entity that authors and
distributes a Modification or New Original Contribution as part of
the Work.

1.7 "You" or "Licensee" means any person or entity exercising rights
under this License.

1.8 "Distribute" means to sell, resell, license, sublicense, publish,
upload, transmit, make available, or otherwise transfer or make
accessible the Software or a Derivative Work to a third party, in
source or object form, for payment or without charge.

1.9 "Notice" means the copyright notice, license text, or
Modification Notice required by this License. "Modification Notice"
means the notice required by Section 3.

1.10 "Material Breach" means a violation of a condition of this
License that substantially defeats a right granted under this
License. Failure to provide a required Modification Notice, or
failure to retain required copyright/license notices, constitutes a
Material Breach.

1.11 "Patent Claim" means a patent claim owned or controlled by the
relevant Licensor or Contributor that is necessarily infringed by
