Software license enforceability varies significantly by jurisdiction.
Warranty disclaimers, liability limitations, automatic-termination
provisions, patent grants, and choice-of-law clauses can all be
subject to mandatory legal rules a private license cannot override —
for example, UK law (Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977) prohibits
